{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set","id":1334440,"title":"Survey: Where is your 3rd ed game set?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-08T06:16:21-07:00","id":1334440,"title":"Survey: Where is your 3rd ed game set?","content":"On the Isle? The Dreaming Sea? The Scavenger Lands? The Cinder Coast?<br /> <br /> I'm just curious as to how popular different areas are for different splat types, and how much people are using the new areas that 3rd ed has introduced.<br /> <br /> Nalak42 (Db) - North<br /> Uknown Darklord - North<br /> BadassOverlord (S) - North<br /> Kerredai - North<br /> BadassOverlord (Db) - North<br /> Zardoz (Db) - North<br /> Satoshi (S) - North<br /> Valles (L) - North<br /> Valles (S) - North<br /> Clophiroth (Db) - North<br /> Epitome (S/L) - Far North-East<br /> DrLoveMonkey (S) - Far North-East<br /> The MG (Db) - North-East<br /> Oz (L) - North-East<br /> Sagara (S) - North-East<br /> The MG (S) - Gloam<br /> Synapse (S/L/Db/Ab) - East<br /> Valles - Scavenger Lands/East<br /> Zardoz (S) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Uknown Darklord - Scavenger Lands<br /> Janissay87 (S) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Sagara (S) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Katana1515 - Scavenger Lands<br /> ArcainOne - Scavenger Lands<br /> Epitome (S) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Dietaku (S/L) - Scavenger Lands<br /> DrLoveMonkey - Scavenger Lands<br /> Taleksi (S/L) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Alucard (S/L/Db) - Scavenger Lands<br /> Pram - Scavenger Lands<br /> Valles (Db) - Dreaming Sea<br /> Epee (S/L/Db) - Dreaming Sea<br /> Kelly (S/Alch) - Dreaming Sea<br /> The MG (DB) - Dreaming Sea<br /> Sagara (S/M) - Dreaming Sea<br /> Chausse - Dreaming Sea<br /> Zardoz (S) - Dreaming Sea<br /> LeTipex (S) - Dreaming Sea<br /> The MG (S) - Dreaming Sea<br /> The MG (S) - South-East (not Dreaming Sea)<br /> Oz (S/L) - South-East (not Dreaming Sea)<br /> Oz (S/L/Db/FF) - South<br /> Katana1515 - South<br /> DrLoveMonkey - South<br /> Sundance - South<br /> BadassOverlord (S) - South<br /> Epitome (S/Db) - South<br /> Clophiroth (L) - South-West<br /> DrLoveMonkey (DB) - South-West and Blessed Isle<br /> The MG (S) - South-West<br /> Clophiroth (Db) - South-West<br /> Kunoichi (S/L/Db) - South-West<br /> BadassOverlord (S) - South-West<br /> BadassOverlord (L) - South-West<br /> Simon (Db/S) - South-West and West<br /> DrLoveMonkey (S) - West<br /> ArcainOne - West<br /> Sith_Happens - West<br /> Synapse (S/L/Db) - West<br /> Pram - West<br /> Alucard (S) - West<br /> DrLoveMonkey - West<br /> The MG (S) - West<br /> Eldagusto (S) - Far North-West.<br /> Zardoz (Db) - Autocthon<br /> Sagara (Db) - Blessed Isle<br /> <br /> (Some of these are previous games no longer running, but I've tried to stick to 3rd edition.)<br /> <br /> What about your groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-19-2019, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T06:21:09-07:00","id":1334441,"title":"","content":"Round-Robin Game (Three Solars, one Lunar, one DB): Scavenger Lands (two stories on the road, two in Nexus)<br /> <br /> Other games are on hold at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T06:26:57-07:00","id":1334442,"title":"","content":"Is your Western game finished or on pause? It sounded like a cool game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T06:34:55-07:00","id":1334444,"title":"","content":"Solar/DB mixed game (4/1) - The South, all over the place, from Kirighast to the elemental pole of fire. Ended recently due to players losing interest.<br /> <br /> Solar/Lunar mixed game (1/1) - The Hundred Kingdoms<br /> <br /> Solar game (3) - A homebrew island of Creation deep in the northeast Wyld. It's essentially a big chunk of North-East territory in terms of weather, wildlife and the kind of people living there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-08-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T06:38:40-07:00","id":1334445,"title":"","content":"Dreaming Sea, mixed party (2 DBs, 4 Solars, 1 Lunar)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T07:10:06-07:00","id":1334452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334442#post1334442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is your Western game finished or on pause? It sounded like a cool game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Misu's player is still interested in finishing the story, but all the other players have dropped due to RL concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T08:35:04-07:00","id":1334463,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's a pity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T09:09:17-07:00","id":1334468,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://thestormthiswaycomes.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Storm This Way Comes</a> has three story threads. <br /> <br /> They're set up to cross sometimes and allow the Chosen to swap out depending on what they want to do. We haven't had a lot of swapping yet, but I think there's some interest.<br /> <br /> Our first main story arc was back and forth with the established DBs and the newly-arriving Solars. This was mostly aimed at introducing the setting, discovering our characters, and so on. We're now into the second arc, which has our story threads pretty well set up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The first thread is mostly Dragon-Blooded. It takes place in the far southwest, starting in a homebrew area called the Stormclaw Dominion. Stormclaw is inland from a coastal mountain formation. This protects it from the constant pounding of thunderstorms-to-hurricanes, drawn inland by the hot air going northward from the Pole of Fire. <br /> <br /> This one was mostly focusing on the experience of being in a guild, with a well-established community around the PCs to support them in their endeavors. We explored backstory with flashbacks to build up on that feeling a bit. One of our Solars swapped in to this thread - the guild was drawn to the northeast into An Teng, to stop an incursion of Abyssal Anathema who were taking over. <br /> <br /> The Solar had been nearly killed by the Satrap of An Teng in her Exaltation backstory, and went back to An Teng as a conqueror. <br /> <br /> We finished up this bit over USA Labor Day weekend (a week ago as of this posting) with a decisive battle for the fate of An Teng. The Abyssals were repulsed at great cost. A conspiracy of Sidereals was hinted at. The Solar discovered that she'd been set up to be killed by her beloved sister. Her sister, secretly a Sidereal, had been convinced that she needed to learn Necromancy to battle the Abyssals and their Deathlord patron.... and that the best sacrifice for that attainment must be the dearest sacrifice. <br /> <br /> The DBs lost their mentor - a well-respected and wise emeritus member of the Wyld Hunt. He'd carefully sheltered the guild through the touchy diplomacy of survival. He was assassinated during the battle by an Abyssal who had, as a mortal, once benefited from his target's mercy. Caught between his command to kill and his feeling of respect, he was in a shrieking limit break and fit of madness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second thread is taking off shortly. Our Solars recovered a skyship at the end of the first arc, and managed to get it to lift off. It desperately needs repairs and refitting to become the Cool Ship which will be the focus of this thread. They're joined by a DB - the swap-character of our Solar from the DB arc. <br /> <br /> The skyship will be the main location, but I'm planning to have it sail north-ish from the Stormclaw area in the far southwest. Thence up to Wu-Jian and over toward Halta in search of repairs and adventure. <br /> <br /> Depending how it plays out, they're likely to have some business to settle with the Deathlord behind the Abyssal incursion into An Teng, but that's far from certain yet.<br /> <br /> Writing for this one, I'm trying to be consistent in playing up the flat shape of Creation. Depending on altitude and weather, you could potentially see from the edge of the world to Meru, or all the way into the mists of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The third thread has just gotten a bit of playtesting. This one is for Lunars, which we're just figuring out. So far, it's been just to knock around some characters during off-game nights when we're missing some players. <br /> <br /> This one is starting off in the southeast, a bit northeast of Prasad. It will probably roam across the Scavenger Lands. Since our Lunars know some NPCs in the other two threads, already, they have ties pulling them west toward An Teng, and north to Nexus and beyond already. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T09:24:48-07:00","id":1334471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334468#post1334468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> The skyship will be the main location, but I'm planning to have it sail north-ish from the Stormclaw area in the far southwest. Thence up to Wu-Jian and over toward Halta in search of repairs and adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a long way!<br /> <br /> We actually did something a little similar ages and ages ago:<br /> We started out in Medo (it wasn't called Medo then, but it was a land of nomadic horsemen that's pretty much where Medo is now), but fled the Wyld Hunt west on my Azure Chariot, then fled the Wyld Hunt again, and ended up in the Haslanti League (too far for them to reach us). (I should mention that our two combat characters died in the first few sessions, hence the fleeing.)<br /> <br /> In the Haslanti League, we got hired for an expedition on an Airship (well, a group of Airships). We travelled west across the North, then across a series of wacky islands (kind of &quot;island-of-the-week&quot;, but with some overarching story threads), trying to beat a Ledaal fleet to an island of sleeping Dragon Kings in the far north-west (turned out the leader of our airship fleet, who we named Admiral Insano for his complete disregard for human life, was actually a Dragon King in disguise and he'd tricked the Haslanti into helping him reach and wake up this ancient city).<br /> Then we travelled south, and our airship was destroyed (always make sure your instructions to bound elementals aren't open to interpretation!). We made it south-east to Coral on a pieced-together wreck. The government of Coral wanted us to take an airship to the Neck on missions for them, but instead we helped overthrow them. Then there was some time-travel shenanigans, and we ended up in Harborhead...<br /> Anyway, travelling across the land by airship actually worked well as a plot. You just need to give people specific reasons to go to different places.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T09:38:27-07:00","id":1334474,"title":"","content":"Oh, I should say, we're actually doing a crossover right now. But I thought I'd say where my games are normally.<br /> <br /> So currently, as well as the game I run every few weeks, I'm playing 3 (each one is monthly) games:<br /> 1) A pocket dimension of floating islands that slowly go from darkness up towards a sun covered in angry faces. They start freezing, as they rise they defrost as do the frozen talking animals on them, until eventually they burn up in the sun. This world was a practice world the Primordials made before Creation.<br /> 2) A jungle land of talking snakes, monkeys and wolves, who were once ruled by humans, until the talking pigs, dogs and geese came across the sea with their trucks, TVs, phones, machine guns and rifles, and killed all humans in order to institute &quot;True Animalism&quot;. Yes, their leader is a pig bureucrat who had his rival pig murdered with an ice pick. And their rivals are the cat-nation who practice Meowism and I assum are led by Chairman Meow.<br /> 3) An island inhabited by frog-people, blue giants, eusocial lizardmen ruled by queens, talking trees, and underground craftsmen who only appear to others dressed in metal suits so no-one knows their true appearance. Instead of a sun, it has a massive central pillar that glows with the colours of one of the Maidens, which it cycles through every few years/decades. It was yellow, and there was an era of trade, but then a Dawn caste warlord arrived and conquered the frog-people, and it turned red. Also, the island is sinking, pushing the five nations to war over dwindling resources. Visions indicate we need to find an Eclipse to captain a giant boat to carry people from each tribe (and 2 of each animal) across the sea to a new land, and this will cause the pillar to turn yellow again and... maybe the pillar will turn yellow again.<br /> <br /> <br /> But these wacky realms probably aren't useful for my survey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:00:40-07:00","id":1334479,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a &quot;hexcrawl&quot;-style game of exploring Creation. The players are all from Autochthonia, where the nation of Nurad has, in desperation, breached the Seal of Eight Divinities with Project Razor in order to collect resources that might let them survive the coming crisis. The portal opened up north of the Dreaming Sea. I won't say exactly where, because at least one player reads the forums, and they haven't actually figured out in-character what part of the Dreaming Sea they're near, and I want that to be a surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:04:54-07:00","id":1334481,"title":"","content":"My game is set in Nexus... with alot of background from the 100 Kingdoms!<br /> <br /> Also had a campaign set with Sunken Clypsis and other First Age relics. Had fun with it for a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:07:45-07:00","id":1334482,"title":"","content":"North West literal corner of the Map. I would count it as west from the perspective of it being in the Far ocean, and Tropical even though its in the North due to Hyperborean style Magic.<br /> <br /> Its Lahat at the End of the World a Continent Region I made up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:39:18-07:00","id":1334488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334479#post1334479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently running a &quot;hexcrawl&quot;-style game of exploring Creation. The players are all from Autochthonia, where the nation of Nurad has, in desperation, breached the Seal of Eight Divinities with Project Razor in order to collect resources that might let them survive the coming crisis. The portal opened up north of the Dreaming Sea. I won't say exactly where, because at least one player reads the forums, and they haven't actually figured out in-character what part of the Dreaming Sea they're near, and I want that to be a surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a lot of fun. I've wanted to do something similar, but with a setting none of my players have any familiarity with. Maybe even randomize the map, or hand off by turns for people to inspire the next hex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:44:22-07:00","id":1334491,"title":"","content":"Kelly, Pram and Eldagusto, out of interest, are your games Solar games?<br /> <br /> It wasn't actually what I was originally thinking about, but I'm interested that there's a lot of mixed games, but no pure-DB games, and only my pure-Lunar game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:49:31-07:00","id":1334492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334488#post1334488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like a lot of fun. I've wanted to do something similar, but with a setting none of my players have any familiarity with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if you want to use Exalted that they know, make sure everyone's playing characters with low Lore, have them roll Lore and when they roll badly it turns out their knowledge of Exalted is completely wrong. So they turn up to, say, Whitewall, and it turns out they were completely wrong about it being run by three gods, that's just a popular legend which outsiders mistake for the truth, and it's actually run by a Raksha warlord. Or whatever.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm doing with my game, but they haven't really realised it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:54:03-07:00","id":1334493,"title":"","content":"My current game (3 Solars, 1 Lunar) is set in the Scavenger Lands, especially the corridor between Great Forks and the Hundred Kingdoms.Considering half our number are Guilders, it makes sense, as we've basically become a Scavenger Lord company of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:09:05-07:00","id":1334496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334491#post1334491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kelly, Pram and Eldagusto, out of interest, are your games Solar games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine started as an all-Solar game (the PCs Exalted soon after arriving in Creation), but the Zenith character was retired relatively soon, and replaced with an Alchemical, which he and I have been homebrewing rules for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:09:50-07:00","id":1334497,"title":"","content":"Our chronicle (4 Solars and 1 Lunar) has mainly taken place in Scavenger Lands / close-East. We've &quot;found&quot; Rathess, thwarted a Vanehan invastion, visited Mahalanka and now our quest to pester the Mask of Winters has taken us to Lost Sarlath, Munaxis and now Yu-Shan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:38:30-07:00","id":1334500,"title":"","content":"North working towards Mantle. Dragonbloods tasked with handling the whole peasant revolt and possibly takeover by a new figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:45:21-07:00","id":1334502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334500#post1334500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">North working towards Mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's Mantle? I don't recognise it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T13:31:58-07:00","id":1334517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334502#post1334502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's Mantle? I don't recognise it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor location mentioned in The Realm.(Pg 83) Really not much said about it, aside from it being a city state, and their queen dealing with a peasant uprising due to oppresive taxes, a famine, and a person claiming to be the illegitimate daughter of the previous queen functioning as a rallying point for the peasant army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:24:49-07:00","id":1334530,"title":"","content":"First game I ran set in the East in a kingdom just to the west of Vaneha, second in a satrapy in the south directly south of the Lap. Then a mortal interlude campaign set in the Blessed Isle and Frosty Dorito Island. Then a player in an archepelago game in the West, and another one in the far far north east. I am currently writing a campaign set on the Isle and Cinder Isles.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should mention they've all be Solars except the mortal one and the one I'm writing which is DB based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-08-2019, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:30:53-07:00","id":1334533,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m currently playing an An-Teng game, and running a game set in Valash, a homebrew celt-inspired kingdom in the Near North (ok. Maybe they are Orlanthi, not Celts). My previous game was set on Tapuru, another homebrew land near the Cinder Isles (in fact, it was the Western tip of the archipielago)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:33:34-07:00","id":1334534,"title":"","content":"Yes it is a Solar Circle, but I'm willing to have it change into a Mixed Circle as people have moved and if I get new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T00:09:31-07:00","id":1334589,"title":"","content":"We have a Full Moon, a Zenith, and a Water Aspect. The game is set in-between Goldenseal and An-Teng on the coast in the South West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T01:07:38-07:00","id":1334593,"title":"","content":"Ah, the An-Teng game is a Lunar one, but the other ones are Dragon-Blooded games: Dynasts in the Valash game, the Outcaste ruling clan in Tapuru","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T02:06:06-07:00","id":1334596,"title":"","content":"Okay, so far there's 2 in the North, 3 in the North-East, 6 in the Scavenger Lands (the two most popular places seem to be Nexus and Vaneha), 2 in the Dreaming Sea, 3 in the South, 4 in the South-West, 2 in the West, 1 in the North-West, and 1 being planned that will be partly in the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised by the dominance of the Scavenger Lands, but maybe not all that surprised. Everywhere else seems roughly the same, with the Cinder Coast and An-Teng slightly more popular. I didn't expect the North-East to be popular, but from the looks of it, like me, the other two I'm guessing chose it because there's not so much there.<br /> <br /> And in terms of characters, it looks like maybe 80% Solars, 10% Lunars, 10% Dragonblood. Something like that (I didn't count carefully). That's a bit different from 2nd ed, where Dynastic games were very popular. I'm guessing it's because the DB book and Realm book just haven't been out for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T05:26:52-07:00","id":1334614,"title":"","content":"No 3E games.<br /> <br /> But I am GMing a game in the north, and playing a Dawn in the Scavenger Lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T06:56:36-07:00","id":1334634,"title":"","content":"I've been running a 3rd Ed Solars game in the South East Scavenger Lands in a homebrew nation named Khaslund (a city state that connects to a few ranch communities and a wasteland north of Ma-Hah's jungle.) Though we've taken a detour to Sijan and had a rivalry with a Guild Hierarch in Great Forks.<br /> <br /> Currently the Wyld Hunt has captured them in the hold of their ship (Horizon Endeavor from Arms) and they're awaiting a visit from a rogue Bronze Faction Siderial that's been warring with / using them to advance her goals against the seven century solar that's been running Khaslund.<br /> <br /> Standard Solar fare, but I'm hoping to kick off its conclusion by the end of 2020; five years is a loooong time to play a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T07:14:05-07:00","id":1334639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334634#post1334634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">five years is a loooong time to play a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> I play a game that's been running.... 12 years? 13?<br /> I ran a game for about 4 years I think, then it went on hiatus, then I ran it again for maybe 2 years after 3rd ed came out, before I finished it. Then my friend took it over because the players wanted to continue, I guess he's run it for a year or 2. So maybe 8 years. Might be more? 9 or 10? I think I started it 12 or 11 years ago, but there were gaps.<br /> I don't dislike either game, they're good, but I really wouldn't mind them ending and starting a new game.<br /> <br /> My new game I've run for, like, 8 sessions. It feels quite different to me because of that. When my game reached essence 5, I found it really difficult to challenge the PCs, whereas now sometimes stuff is actually quite hard for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T10:21:21-07:00","id":1334669,"title":"","content":"One in Chiaroscuro (S), two in the North (S and DB) and two in the Caul (S and L).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T11:09:57-07:00","id":1334684,"title":"","content":"Played in one in Chiarascuro, ran one in the Scavenger Lands, mostly focused on Great Forks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T12:21:06-07:00","id":1334697,"title":"","content":"I ran a solo game set in Y'danna down in the Dreaming Sea (starring a Solar), and then a Solar game set in the Southwest.<br /> <br /> As for games I've played, there was a Solar game set in Gloam and a DB game (pre-WFHW) that saw the characters travel around the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> Finally, my currently active games, for a given value of <i>active</i>, are a Lunar game in Wu Jian, a Solar game in the Southeast (but far from the Dreaming Sea), and a solo DB game in some nonspecific part of the North.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T15:02:52-07:00","id":1334716,"title":"","content":"As people keep saying games they used to play, then assuming they're 3rd ed I've just put them up as well. Ideally I guess it should be weighted towards longer-running games, but that's too difficult.<br /> <br /> So it looks like the Scavenger Lands is most popular (10), followed by the South-West (8), South (7), North (6), Dreaming Sea (5), West (5), North-East (3). Hardly anyone runs games on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see the South-West with its new stuff is so popular, though I'm surprised, I thought people would be more into the Dreaming Sea than the Cinder Coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T17:07:39-07:00","id":1334737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334639#post1334639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't dislike either game, they're good, but I really wouldn't mind them ending and starting a new game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seriously need to convince your group to do that, man. If you can convince them to do a DB game it's even better. You might even have a debate occasionally about possibly making a compromise with an NPC or something, and somebody might get crashed in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T20:45:09-07:00","id":1334762,"title":"","content":"I narrate a game in the West (Azure, specifically, on the brink of war with Skullstone) and play a game in the East (we're colonizers taming a wild land and improving on the relics of a bygone era). Both games have solars, dbs and lunars. The Eastern game technically has an abyssal, we're using a fan port.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 09-09-2019, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:35:58-07:00","id":1334791,"title":"","content":"When you say East, do you actually mean in the eastern forest?<br /> <br /> Because so far you're the only person to do that. I think the Eastern forest and jungle empires are the least played area. Over 12 years of playing Exalted, I've played in the West, An-Teng, South, South-East (but not Dreaming Sea), all over the Scavenger Lands, North-East, North, North-West (Coral, etc) and the Blessed Isle. But never further east than Greyfalls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You seriously need to convince your group to do that, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of did. I started a new 0xp Lunar game. But we've got 4 games going on Sundays: the 300xp game in Egypt-expy land, the 450xp game in the lakes near Harborhead, my new Lunar game, and a Dragonblood game I don't play. So they alternate.<br /> They also started a new game for 3rd edition, which is on Fridays I think.<br /> So for nearly all the players, they actually are playing a new (well, E3 now, but that's pretty reasonable) Solar game and a very new Lunar game. But I'm only running a new game (which I'm really enjoying actually).<br /> <br /> One of my STs (the Egypt-expy game) actually did say he wants to end his game at some point. But I guess he wants to tie up all the plot strands and stuff, which is understandable (the current plot is actually really good, I'm just bored of the PCs because they've been mostly the same for 12 years). And as it's currently on break while we do crossovers, even if he did that fairly quickly (in like 10 sessions), with monthly games, we'd be talking end of next year. But it's probably more like 2 years I guess.<br /> <br /> The DB ST also wants to end his Dragonblood game, and he says they're in the last story arc, but again they're on break while we do crossovers, and then 1 session a week means we're talking end of next year at the earliest, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so it's not a priority for most of the players because they're playing one new and one fairly new (like 2 years I guess) game, but I don't play any (I run one). The ST of the 450xp game says that essentially he has plot ideas for characters he knows and so he wants to keep that game going, because those are the characters he knows well.<br /> I think it would be better if we all fell into a big XP-void that sucked out all our XP and turned us into starting characters.<br /> Because then, as you say, we <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> might even have a debate occasionally about possibly making a compromise with an NPC or something. </div> </div> </div>Some of the characters are kind of annoying, but I think it's 90% because they'll never compromise with NPCs or each other (which has led to issues with them refusing to work together, which is very annoying as at what point we were split into 5 groups, which really cuts down on each person's play-time), and that would help. It's very difficult to argue that a guy with Supernal Resistance should compromise when he's virtually unkillable. Or the woman with Death Ray.<br /> But I doubt people would be up for that.<br /> <br /> I also think as they all play a Dragonblood game currently, when that one ends they probably won't want to play a new one. My Lunars game got people interested because we'd only ever done one all-Lunars game before, like 7 years ago, and it didn't last very long. Actually, we used to do tons and tons and tons of Dynastic games, so I'm not that psyched to do one, nor I think would others. Maybe Dragonblood Outcastes.<br /> <br /> But honestly, with 5 exalted games running, if one or two finish, while I would like to do a new Exalted game I'd probably more like to play a 40k game or superheroes or sci-fi or urban fantasy or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-10-2019, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:10:05-07:00","id":1334803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334791#post1334791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say East, do you actually mean in the eastern forest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhmm, somewhere between the Lair of Ma-ha-suchi and Rathess, just west of Ixcoatli, and the place plays a role in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:14:01-07:00","id":1334805,"title":"","content":"Cool. Simon Darkstep said he's planning to eventually send his players to Halta, but it looks currently like you're the only person here playing a game set in the actual East.<br /> <br /> <br /> Before settling on the snowy lands of the North-East north of Iscomay, the big North-East forest was my second choice for a setting. Forests that go on for huge distances are something Exalted has that most settings don't, but people don't seem to use it much. I guess maybe people don't know what to do with it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:42:39-07:00","id":1334815,"title":"","content":"What would someone do with a bunch of trees, right?<br /> <br /> A good start is cutting them down.<br /> Cutting wood is as much a local activity as an international one, and the setting's technological era allows for it: cargo ships in the lower hundreds of tons, immense beasts of burden, wide-reaching empires and well established trade between all major hubs mean that Eastern woods can be relatively cheap to import, especially those with properties uncommon elsewhere. There should be hundreds or thousands of villages and towns specialized in exporting wood, especially along the two gargantuan rivers on the southeast and northeast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T04:51:44-07:00","id":1334819,"title":"","content":"My 2 first campaigns were set in the South-East, close to Palanquin, along the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> I'm intending to run a new campaign on a Huge City Boat created by the players in one of those earlier campaign, and use it to travel a bit the Dreaming Sea and possibly try to make them travel somewhere else in Creation, like the SouthWest or just West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T05:11:15-07:00","id":1334824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334815#post1334815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would someone do with a bunch of trees, right?<br /> <br /> A good start is cutting them down.<br /> Cutting wood is as much a local activity as an international one, and the setting's technological era allows for it: cargo ships in the lower hundreds of tons, immense beasts of burden, wide-reaching empires and well established trade between all major hubs mean that Eastern woods can be relatively cheap to import, especially those with properties uncommon elsewhere. There should be hundreds or thousands of villages and towns specialized in exporting wood, especially along the two gargantuan rivers on the southeast and northeast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... it's kind of obvious actually, I have considered that before, but you've given me an idea. I would like, later in the game, to possibly move my PCs down to Iscomay (if they want to) and the forests that surround it. One PC comes from a fire-manse inside that forest (giving that area more of a jungle feel) that the Guild tried to invade and loot. He and another PC hate the Guild. So I could probably do stuff with the local spirits and animals complaining about devastating Guild logging operations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T17:44:48-07:00","id":1335009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334824#post1334824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm... it's kind of obvious actually, I have considered that before, but you've given me an idea. I would like, later in the game, to possibly move my PCs down to Iscomay (if they want to) and the forests that surround it. One PC comes from a fire-manse inside that forest (giving that area more of a jungle feel) that the Guild tried to invade and loot. He and another PC hate the Guild. So I could probably do stuff with the local spirits and animals complaining about devastating Guild logging operations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly what happened in Underfoots backstory , the Guild Expedition fleet gone up river and started major deforestation effort to set up local logging base to fund further exploration and major deforestation being his first encounter with people is the reason why he doesn\u2019t like people and guild in particular . Safe to say he burned their ships and the Great white Apes \ud83e\udd8d ate all the loggers . I doubt anyone made it out alive unless they somehow survived the perilous journey on foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T23:00:55-07:00","id":1335032,"title":"","content":"The Solars game went from Nexus/Celeren/Lookshy (E) to the NE homebrew city of Lighthalzen, whereas the Lunars games is set in Chiaroscuro (S)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T07:05:47-07:00","id":1335108,"title":"","content":"I have to say, it's fun reading about everyone's campaigns. <br /> <br /> My solar campaign is set on the western coast of the Dreaming Sea. It's currently on hold due to RL reasons.<br /> <br /> And I'm planning a massive DB campaign set mainly on the Blessed Isle and around a few sattrapies (Notably Yirji!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T07:13:33-07:00","id":1335110,"title":"","content":"Where's Yirji?<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is interesting. I notice for example that there's plenty of games where people are playing Solars, Lunars and Dragonblood together; evidently the power difference isn't a huge hurdle.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to see some of the wackier stuff, like islands in the Wyld, Autocthonians exploring Creation, Dynasts in Autochthon, or a giant boat-city.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested to see that most people seem to play/have played multiple games, which is good. It shows a vibrancy to the fanbase I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-11-2019, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T07:14:45-07:00","id":1335111,"title":"","content":"games I have run:<br /> Solar game that traveled the entire world<br /> Solar game in the Haslanti leauge<br /> <br /> Games I have played in:<br /> Mortals/Solars in the Dreaming Sea<br /> DBs on the Blessed Isle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T09:09:24-07:00","id":1335132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1335110#post1335110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also interested to see that most people seem to play/have played multiple games, which is good. It shows a vibrancy to the fanbase I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unfortunately, at least in my case, all those former games are also <i>lost</i> games, ended before their time for various reasons (the Gloam game being the worst one, as it ended due to the year 2016 in general).<br /> <br /> The only completed Exalted game I've been in was in 2e, and so not accounted for here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T09:18:57-07:00","id":1335133,"title":"","content":"What do we mean by completed games? I think most games just go and go and go and then... stop. I've seen a few games that ended with a deliberate finale, but most just carried on and on until people got bored or something. Or continued indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T12:09:11-07:00","id":1335177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1335133#post1335133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we mean by completed games? I think most games just go and go and go and then... stop. I've seen a few games that ended with a deliberate finale, but most just carried on and on until people got bored or something. Or continued indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually my games last a couple years until we make something else. Grandiose, definitive endings are rare, but the open stories are finished. Leto's story ended after a series of war events where the death tolls scaled up and up and then he claimed every single corpse as a servant that he then took to his fortress of ice. Monsoon Dancer's story ended when she killed yet another petty tyrant that terrorized her beloved wu-jian, but then crowned herself &quot;queen of all that shit&quot; and people accepted. Ivory Wasp's ended when she was blinded in a fight against a grave behemoth, decided her previous path of piety was not netting proper results and became a wanderer on the wasting tundra, a destructive spectre hounding the icewalkers forevermore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T12:19:32-07:00","id":1335179,"title":"","content":"That's good, I find generally it's more satisfying to have a game that ends properly, with a distinct victory, than just carries on and on until the ST/Players get bored.<br /> I've seen a number of games that got to a really good finale... and then continued, and were kind of bleh.<br /> <br /> With my 2nd ed game, I realised it had become like that, so I decided to have a big finale (saving the world, etc), and it worked much better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T12:45:35-07:00","id":1335180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1335179#post1335179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's good, I find generally it's more satisfying to have a game that ends properly, with a distinct victory, than just carries on and on until the ST/Players get bored.<br /> I've seen a number of games that got to a really good finale... and then continued, and were kind of bleh.<br /> <br /> With my 2nd ed game, I realised it had become like that, so I decided to have a big finale (saving the world, etc), and it worked much better.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My recently ended game went something like that. We spent ~2 irl years making a name for ourselves in the South and solving every problem there, culminating with taking down Ahlat and setting up a river Goddess in his stead.<br /> <br /> Then the Circle started heading West to continue the main Campaign, which was meant to take us across all of Creation. But it felt like the story we'd actually become invested in was already over, so the game just sort of petered out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T13:47:33-07:00","id":1335190,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I did a DnD game once where we working up to a big heist over about a year, it was really good, and then I had to go to London for 3 months. When I came back, they'd done the big heist... but the game was really... meh? Sometimes the ST would retconn stuff, or move stuff around, or bring some pre-genned characters for us to play for a session. He moved us to a new city, with a new plot... and then one day came in and shouted at us for 10 minutes because of something some people hadn't understood the previous session, told us all to make new characters, and then after the game facebooked us to say he was stepping down as ST. I talked to him later and he said he really hadn't enjoyed it since we finished the big finale plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it felt like the story we'd actually become invested in was already over, </div> </div> </div>I think one thing here is, because you're moving to a new situation, all the NPCs your characters have made alliance with are gone, and all their achievements feel maybe redundant? Because you've brought peace to the land and so forth, but now you've gone somewhere else where that hasn't happened.<br /> <br /> (Our two main antagonists are Ahlat and his empire, and the Realm. Replacing him with a different god sounds like a plan. And I can think of just the one...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T15:14:24-07:00","id":1335201,"title":"","content":"All of my games for the past few years have had definitive endings, usually ones that had been planned out from the start of the game. Usually I start things off by introducing small, easily solved problems, things that take 1-3 sessions to fix and then they\u2019re fixed and it\u2019s a solid victory. So I\u2019ll start with a few of them, get the players used to the world and building interactions, then move onto some bigger problems with longer arcs, then even longer arcs that take multiple stories to complete. So they\u2019ll get a solid victory, but that victory won\u2019t defeat their current antagonist. And then for the last one or two they\u2019re big huge sweeping arcs with several smaller adventures and a lot more complex problems that are more me going \u201chere, you guys have a lot of power and connections now, figure this one out.\u201d As well as the players taking a lot more active roles in how things go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T05:59:07-07:00","id":1335302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1335110#post1335110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's Yirji?<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is interesting. I notice for example that there's plenty of games where people are playing Solars, Lunars and Dragonblood together; evidently the power difference isn't a huge hurdle.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to see some of the wackier stuff, like islands in the Wyld, Autocthonians exploring Creation, Dynasts in Autochthon, or a giant boat-city.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested to see that most people seem to play/have played multiple games, which is good. It shows a vibrancy to the fanbase I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>My multiple games is mostly that I had to move cities and now I live in another province. So, I play one game on Saturdays with my local players, and some Tuesdays I play with my old players on Skype :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T08:38:17-07:00","id":1335317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1334697#post1334697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]a solo DB game in some nonspecific part of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div> I asked the ST, and it turns it out it's set in the Northeast, largely north of Chanta and east of Icehome.<br /> <br /> As for what I meant by &quot;completed&quot; games... Anything that doesn't feel <i>unfinished</i>, really. If it has <i>something</i> like an ending, or the group agrees that they're satisfied, a game can be said to be complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T08:42:53-07:00","id":1335319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1334440-survey-where-is-your-3rd-ed-game-set?p=1335302#post1335302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My multiple games is mostly that I had to move cities and now I live in another province. So, I play one game on Saturdays with my local players, and some Tuesdays I play with my old players on Skype :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of thing is probably the case for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> I play DnD with my friends in Brighton, where I live, and play Exalted over Skype with my old friends from university. But for some reason we've ended up doing 5 Exalted games, each game generally 1/month, rather than 1 or 2. I think it's generally because people have had new ideas for games and haven't wanted to end the old ones. For example, when I had the idea for a Lunar game, I thought I should wait until some of the other games ended but the players said it'd be better to start while people were still excited by the new book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:03:27-07:00","id":1335612,"title":"","content":"My Solar campaign is set in the North, and has been fairly wide-ranging in that direction; the Circle's home base is near the northern part of the Haslanti league, but they've gone as far south as Medo and are currently in Whitewall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T14:43:46-07:00","id":1335794,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a Lunars game set in the North, and have in the past run a Solar one near Ma-Ha-Suchi's neck of the woods. I've participated as a player in a northern Solars game and a Prasadi DB one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T22:28:27-07:00","id":1335840,"title":"","content":"Current game I\u2019m in is... we know it\u2019s further west than Wavecrest but have never definitely settled on a latitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T00:28:14-07:00","id":1335999,"title":"","content":"The current game I'm running is set in the deep south, based pretty firmly around Gem, apart from a quick excursion up the Diamond Road and another to Goldenseal. After the first big plotline is finished, though, I expect the story to make its way to the coast around Zhaojun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:02:45-07:00","id":1336678,"title":"","content":"I've two Solar campaigns going on. <br /> <br /> First and oldest is located in Wavecrest, specifically Windgate and Goldsails. Players are currently working to gather support for Wavecrest to abandon their connection with the realm while facing known threat of pirate armada from coral and the unknown threat of Abyssal Captains hunting down legendary artifacts to supplement their secret Armada in Skullstone. Mean while one of the dragon blooded houses is planning on using Wavecrest as a bug out territory and are trying to take full control of the region with out raising suspicions back home.<br /> <br /> The Second campaign is in... Lookshy. Yep... a full solar circle who calls the city of Dragon Blooded home. We have a few born and bred Lookshian citizens who ultimately believe that Lookshy is the greatest city that represents freedom of the river province despite their attitude towards Solars. We are playing a a lot with the purists vs everyone else as one of the players has effectively been ousted as a Solar already. Pulling from 2nd edition's attitude toward solar exalted (they are tolorated until they are dangerous) plus the idea that Lookshy deal with their problem citizens themselves. The ousted character has become a tool for Lookshy rather than execution on the Chumyo's orders and the effects that will have on Lookshy as a Dragon Blooded / Shogunate / old school immaculate faith / second age mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12317-arcainone","name":"ArcainOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T05:04:32-07:00","id":1336826,"title":"","content":"Solars in Lookshy is definitely a bit different!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T06:27:42-07:00","id":1336851,"title":"","content":"Okay, so it's gone a little quieter, so I'll round up the results (though more people can feel free to post).<br /> <br /> 10 games in the North<br /> 5 games in the North-East<br /> 1 or 2 in the East proper<br /> 12 in the Scavenger Lands<br /> 11 in the South-East, 9 of them around the Dreaming Sea.<br /> 6 in the South<br /> 7 or 8 in the South-West<br /> 8 in the West<br /> And a few in other places; 1 in Autocthon, 1 in Gloam, 1 on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> Solar games are the most popular, followed by mixed games... that tend to be mostly Solars.<br /> <br /> There are 10 Dragonblood games (which are mostly not on the Blessed Isle, but are a bit). There are 4 Lunar games... none of which, interestingly, are in the Scavenger Lands or Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> I guess this probably reflects the amount of time that the splatbooks have been out,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}